entry.summary:
When visible breadcrumb links and JSON-LD structured data drift apart over time, search crawlers may encounter conflicting hierarchy signals that complicate indexing and degrade user trust.
Quick solution:
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Home",
      "item": "https://example.com/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Articles",
      "item": "https://example.com/articles/"
    }
  ]
}

Prerequisites include maintaining an ordered array structure in your backend or static site generator. A common caution is that structured data eligibility does not guarantee a rich result or a click-through rate improvement, as outlined in the …
